Z||000000||Robert||05-29-2001||10:22 PM||||I'm having a problem with my computer.  If you have @home, please look at this site and tell me if you see a page that says "wrong", or the web site for Walnut Creek Racquet Club.<BR>Thanks<BR>Robert<BR>PS<BR>I'm only asking because my computer only sees "wrong", and everyone thinks it's @homes's fault.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||sjp777||05-29-2001||10:28 PM||||You didn't post the url||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||05-29-2001||10:38 PM||||The problem Robert is having is resolving <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net," TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net,</A>  which reverse resolves to ns19.zabco.net. He brought this up in another thread a couple of days ago. <P>Robert, the reason everybody is telling you the problem is with @home is simply because the problem **IS** with @home.  The DNS server you're resolving against has bad data in its cache.  I fatfingered the urls in my other response but the actual data is correct. <P>Anyone else out there is welcome to try to resolve <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net," TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net,</A>  it'll resolve to 139.142.181.119.  Then set your DNS server to 24.20.31.178, and again try to resolve <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net," TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net,</A>  it'll return a non-authoritative result (i.e. its getting the value from its internal cache) of 207.150.192.12. <P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sjp777:<BR><B>You didn't post the url</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Robert||05-29-2001||10:44 PM||||Sorry for the no url post....<BR>Yes, I am having a problem with <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net." TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net.</A> <BR>I thougt if other people using @home can see the site, then it's "my" problem.  If other @home users see "Wrong", then it's @home's problem.<BR>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||LarryB||05-29-2001||10:50 PM||||This is from a Solaris 2.7 box.  It shows what I'm talking about.<P>shell2% nslookup<BR>Default Server:  ns1.xcom.net<BR>Address:  209.244.125.4<P>&gt; <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A> <BR>Server:  ns1.xcom.net<BR>Address:  209.244.125.4<P>Name:    ns19.wcrc.net<BR>Address:  139.142.181.119<BR>Aliases:  <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A> <P>&gt; 139.142.181.119<BR>Server:  ns1.xcom.net<BR>Address:  209.244.125.4<P>Name:    ns19.zabco.net<BR>Address:  139.142.181.119<P>&gt; server 24.20.31.178<BR>Default Server:  proxy1.wntck1.sfba.home.com<BR>Address:  24.20.31.178<P>Non-authoritative answer:<BR>Name:    <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A> <BR>Address:  207.150.192.12<P>&gt; 207.150.192.12<BR>Server:  proxy1.wntck1.sfba.home.com<BR>Address:  24.20.31.178<P>*** proxy1.wntck1.sfba.home.com can't find 207.150.192.12: Server failed<BR>&gt; 139.142.181.119<BR>Server:  proxy1.wntck1.sfba.home.com<BR>Address:  24.20.31.178<P>Name:    ns19.zabco.net<BR>Address:  139.142.181.119<P>&gt; exit<BR>shell2%     <BR>||||reg||1
