Z||000007||jlruiz67||05-30-2001||12:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Robert:<BR><B>Larry<BR>I'm on hold with @home level2 right now (15min).  Can you explain why Phil can see the page and I can not?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I have @home and I can load the page as well...<P>It could be that we are using diferent DNS servers<P>  Connection-specific DNS Suffix  . : alsv1.occa.home.com<BR>  IP Address. . . . . . . . . . . . : 24.0.***.***<BR>  Subnet Mask . . . . . . . . . . . : 255.255.255.0<BR>  Default Gateway . . . . . . . . . : 24.0.208.1<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||RNGCRSH||05-30-2001||12:27 AM||||I have @home. I got the same problem<P>found a workaround, go to wcrc.net without the "www" at the begining.<P>when you get to thier site you will notice they have a message that says that they are in the process of moving to new servers.<P>thier new ip addresses most likely have not been registered with all of the DNS's out there yet.<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||LarryB||05-30-2001||12:34 AM||||Different name/proxy servers.<P>A large network like @home will have multiple server pairs distributed throughout the US for both redundancy and performance reasons.  Depending on where you live you may have different servers.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jlruiz67:<BR><B> <BR>I have @home and I can load the page as well...<P>It could be that we are using diferent DNS servers<P>  Connection-specific DNS Suffix  . : alsv1.occa.home.com<BR>  IP Address. . . . . . . . . . . . : 24.0.***.***<BR>  Subnet Mask . . . . . . . . . . . : 255.255.255.0<BR>  Default Gateway . . . . . . . . . : 24.0.208.1<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||LarryB||05-30-2001||12:38 AM||||wcnc.net has a time to live value of 30 minutes, so any DNS server that has cached the info should flush it out of the cache after a maximum of 30 minutes. <P>Here's an example, the value will be flushed in about 28 minutes from the DNS server 209.244.125.4 (one of my DNS servers)<P>shell2% dig <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A> <P>; &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; DiG 8.2 &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A>  <BR>;; res options: init recurs defnam dnsrch<BR>;; got answer:<BR>;; -&gt;&gt;HEADER&lt;&lt;- opcode: QUERY, status: NOERROR, id: 6<BR>;; flags: qr rd ra; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 2, AUTHORITY: 2, ADDITIONAL: 2<BR>;; QUERY SECTION:<BR>;;      <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net," TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net,</A>  type = A, class = IN<P>;; ANSWER SECTION: <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net." TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net.</A>            28m15s IN CNAME  ns19.wcrc.net.<BR>ns19.wcrc.net.          28m15s IN A     139.142.181.119<P>;; AUTHORITY SECTION:<BR>wcrc.net.               19h34m51s IN NS  NS1.ZABCO.net.<BR>wcrc.net.               19h34m51s IN NS  NS2.ZABCO.net.<P>;; ADDITIONAL SECTION:<BR>NS1.ZABCO.net.          21h33m1s IN A   139.142.181.101<BR>NS2.ZABCO.net.          21h33m1s IN A   207.153.9.203<P>;; Total query time: 9 msec<BR>;; FROM: shell2 to SERVER: default -- 209.244.125.4<BR>;; WHEN: Wed May 30 00:36:39 2001<BR>;; MSG SIZE  sent: 30  rcvd: 139<P>shell2% <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RNGCRSH:<BR><B>I have @home. I got the same problem<P>found a workaround, go to wcrc.net without the "www" at the begining.<P>when you get to thier site you will notice they have a message that says that they are in the process of moving to new servers.<P>thier new ip addresses most likely have not been registered with all of the DNS's out there yet.<P>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 05-30-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
