Z||000013||thomas_l||05-30-2001||09:50 AM||||Maybe @home had a lazy DNS server - I get the correct addy from work both with & without the www alias:<P>C:\&gt;nslookup -querytype=ANY <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A> <BR>Server:  wouldntyouliketoknow.net<BR>Address:  127.0.0.1<P>Non-authoritative answer: <A HREF="http://www.wcrc.net" TARGET=_blank>www.wcrc.net</A>     canonical name = ns19.wcrc.net<P>ns19.wcrc.net   internet address = 139.142.181.119<P>C:\&gt;nslookup -querytype=ANY wcrc.net<BR>Server:  wouldntyouliketoknow.net<BR>Address:  127.0.0.1<P>Non-authoritative answer:<BR>wcrc.net        nameserver = ns1.zabco.net<BR>wcrc.net        nameserver = ns2.zabco.net<BR>wcrc.net        internet address = 139.142.181.119<P>wcrc.net        nameserver = ns1.zabco.net<BR>wcrc.net        nameserver = ns2.zabco.net<BR>ns1.zabco.net   internet address = 139.142.181.101<BR>ns2.zabco.net   internet address = 207.153.9.203||||reg||1
Z||000014||Robert||05-31-2001||07:06 PM||||Just an update on what happened the last few days.   As the tennis season started, we received 6 different complaints of not being able to access the site.  Guess what?  All the complainers had @home.  I had each of them call @home and complain.  Today I am happy to say I can see the new site through @home.  Of course, @home says there was nothing wrong with the system, must have been my operating system.<BR>Thank you all for you help, the process is just as nice as the outcome.<BR>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."<P>Will Rogers, U.S. Writer and Humorist||||reg||10
